---
title: Risotto alla Milanese
servings: 4
tags: [italian, rice, vegetarian, comfort food]
source: https://github.com/cooklang/cookcli
description: A creamy saffron risotto from Milan. The key is patience and good stock.
---

= Prepare the base =

Finely dice the @onion{1}. Warm the @vegetable stock{1%l} in a #saucepan{} and keep it at a gentle simmer.

> Homemade stock makes a big difference here.

Dissolve the @saffron threads{1%pinch} in @water{2%tbsp}(warm) and set aside.

= Cook the rice =

Melt @butter{30%g} in a #large heavy-bottomed pan{} over a medium heat. Add the diced onion and cook for ~onion softening{5%minutes}, until translucent but not browned.

Add the @arborio rice{320%g} and stir for ~rice toasting{2%minutes}, until the edges of the grains turn translucent.

Pour in the @white wine{100%ml} and stir until absorbed.

Add a ladleful of warm stock and stir until it is absorbed, then add another. Keep going for ~risotto cooking{18%minutes}, adding stock gradually and stirring often.

> Patience: stir often and add the stock slowly.

= Finish =

Take the pan off the heat. Add the saffron water, the @parmesan cheese{60%g}(finely grated) and @butter{20%g}(cold), and stir vigorously until creamy. This is the mantecatura.

Season with @salt{} and @black pepper{} to taste.

Cover and rest for ~resting{2%minutes}, then serve on warm plates.
